stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Ungraded: new assertion enters register
    Ungraded --> Hypothesis: default on entry - unmarked is a defect

    Hypothesis --> Verified: primary source captured and survives hostile re-check incl. corrigendum step
    Hypothesis --> Killed: §20 kill criterion fires or primary source contradicts
    Hypothesis --> Hypothesis: refined - range tightens, still unvalidated

    Ungraded --> Verified: blocked capture resolved by a different method - EV-009
    Verified --> Verified: re-verified - date arrives, source still holds
    Verified --> Hypothesis: auto-demote - re-verify date passed with no re-check
    Verified --> Killed: amendment, corrigendum or superseding instrument - EPF Act 1952 repeal 21 Nov 2025

    Killed --> [*]: terminal - stays on §20 blocklist

    note right of Verified
        Verified as of a date only.
        Carries a re-verify trigger.
        Dated forced checks include
        EPF/ESI savings expiry ~21.11.2026,
        DPDP commencement ~13.05.2027,
        Form 138 Q4 format and due date.
        Mirror-read rows are Verified - mirror
        until pulled from the primary source.
    end note

    note right of Killed
        Does not revive. A resurrected
        quantity re-enters as a NEW claim
        with a NEW ID and its own grading,
        e.g. EPF Scheme 2026 as EV-003.
        A conclusion drawn from a killed
        claim is marked Reversed.
        Rule version archived, not erased,
        for retrospective recompute.
    end note
